3:This document provides a complete technical reference for the **`swegemma`** evaluation harness and its companion libraries (**`adk-submission`** and **`adk-eval-core`**). It explains how competitor submissions are validated and compiled, how the harness orchestrates agent sessions and sandboxes, how the built-in tools behave, and how generated patches are extracted and graded.
7:## Table of Contents
16:8. [Patch Extraction & Phase 2 Verification (`verify_task`)](#8-patch-extraction--phase-2-verification-verify_task)
22:## 1. System Architecture & Library Stack
29:| **`adk-eval-core`** | **Core Evaluation Infrastructure.** Provides base task/result models (`BenchmarkTask`, `BaseTaskResult`, `EvaluationResult`), sandbox execution backends (`DockerContainer`, `SubprocessSandbox`), resilient 3-tier file editing (`apply_replacement`), token/cost tracking (`TokenBudget`, `PricingTable`), ADK plugins (`EventDisplayPlugin`, `ModelRetryPlugin`), and ATIF v1.7 trajectory tracing (`SessionTrace`). |
30:| **`swegemma`** | **SWE-bench Harness & Scoring Engine.** Implements the two-container SWE evaluation lifecycle (`Evaluator`, `run_agent_sandbox`, `verify_task`), binds the 9 sandboxed workspace and code-intelligence tools (`SwegemmaContext.create_tools()`), constructs the task prompt and continuation nudges, extracts unified git diffs (`scripts/inference.py`), and runs hermetic `pytest` + JUnit XML verification (`scripts/metric.py`). |
48:    subgraph Sandboxes["Isolated Per-Task Sandboxes"]
49:        ContA["Container A: Agent Sandbox (/workspace)\nSnapshot + Editable Install + Baseline Commit"]
50:        ContB["Container B: Verification Sandbox (/workspace)\nFresh Snapshot + agent_patch + test_patch + pytest"]
66:## 2. Submission Contract & Declarative Agent Schema (`adk-submission`)
68:### 2.1. Declarative-Only Security Model
69:Competitors **do not** submit Python code entrypoints (`agent.py` or `agent_fn`). Standard ADK's `from_config()` permits arbitrary dynamic Python imports; **`adk-submission` replaces it with a sandboxed YAML compiler (`compile_submission`)**. All agents, sub-agents, workflows, tools, and generation parameters are declared in YAML and resolved against closed host registries (`ToolRegistry`, `ModelRegistry`, `SkillRegistry`, `CallbackRegistry`).
71:### 2.2. Submission Directory Layout
99:- **Sandboxed `!include` Directive**: YAML files may embed external files using `!include <relative_path>`:
104:### 2.3. Supported Agent Classes (`agent_class`)
105:`SandboxedAgentConfig` supports four discriminated agent types (defaulting to `LlmAgent` if `agent_class` is omitted):
127:### 2.4. Enforced Structural Limits & Generation Constraints
128:Submission constraints in `swegemma` (`build_submission_limits()` in `swegemma/config.py`) are intentionally minimal: **aside from security sandboxing (no symlinks, no path traversal, declarative YAML only), the primary hard constraint is a total unpacked submission size of `< 3 GiB` (`3,221,225,472` bytes), including all `adapters/` weights**, plus token ceilings required by the 4x L4 GPU context window (`32,768` tokens).
154:> Execution-altering ADK fields that bypass the sandbox (`tools`, `system_instruction`, `http_options`, `safety_settings`, or `response_schema` inside `generate_content_config`) are excluded from `GenerateContentConfig` by schema design and will raise a validation error if set.
158:## 3. Model Registry, Single-Model Rule & LoRA Adapters on 4x L4 GPUs
160:### 3.1. Computational Environment: 4x NVIDIA L4 GPUs (96 GB Total VRAM)
184:4. **Host Container Sandboxing (`4 GiB` RAM / `2 vCPUs` per container)**: Prevents repository test suites inside `Container A` and `Container B` from starving the host CPU or system RAM needed by the vLLM engine.
186:### 3.2. The Single Base Model Rule
191:### 3.3. Pre-Registered Model Aliases & Routing
204:### 3.4. Multi-LoRA Serving (`adapters/`) & Sizing Guidelines
219:## 4. Two-Phase Evaluation Lifecycle
221:Every benchmark task (`Task`) is evaluated in **two completely separate sandbox lifecycles** (`Container A` for agent execution and `Container B` for verification).
226:    participant ContA as Container A (Agent Sandbox)
228:    participant ContB as Container B (Verification Sandbox)
230:    Eval->>ContA: 1. Start sandbox & setup wheels
242:    Note over Eval,ContB: If agent_patch is non-empty (or no agent_error), proceed to Phase 2
251:### 4.1. Sandbox Hardware & Isolation (`ContainerManager` vs `SubprocessManager`)
252:- **Docker Backend (`--sandbox docker`, default)**:
253:  - Image: `swebench-sandbox:latest`
259:- **Subprocess Backend (`--sandbox subprocess`, used in environments without a Docker daemon)**:
260:  - Creates an isolated temporary directory `swegemma_sandbox_<id>_` with `workspace/`, `tmp/`, `wheels/`, and an isolated virtual environment `venv/`.
261:  - Rewrites shell references to `/workspace`, `/tmp`, `/wheels`, and `/usr/local/bin` to the sandbox directory paths and executes commands in a new process group (`start_new_session=True`), terminating the full process group (`os.killpg(..., signal.SIGKILL)`) on command timeout.
263:### 4.2. Container Bootstrap Sequence (`container_setup.py`)
266:1. **Wheel Staging (`setup_container_wheels`)**: Prepares `/wheels` inside the sandbox.
283:5. **Test Dependency Installation (`install_test_dependencies`)**: Streams cached unpacked site-packages (`<20 MB` base wheels and `>=20 MB` workspace-imported wheels) into the container Python environment and runs `/sandbox/setup.py --fast-path <repo>`.
294:## 5. Harness-to-Agent Interaction Protocol
296:### 5.1. Session State Variables
297:When `run_agent_sandbox` creates the ADK session (`app_name='swegemma_eval'`, `user_id='eval_user'`), it populates `session.state` with:
303:### 5.2. Initial User Prompt (`build_agent_prompt`)
337:   - *Note on in-sandbox testing*: By default, `enable_sandbox_testing = True` is active in `EvalConfig` and `agent_runner.py`, so `pytest` and `unittest` are available inside Container A and Instruction `3` reads: `"3. Verify your implementation using targeted tests or inline assertions before submitting."` (If `enable_sandbox_testing` is explicitly set to `False`, the harness masks `pytest` and `unittest` inside Container A and adjusts Instruction `3` to advise inline `python3 -c "..."` assertions).
349:### 5.3. Multi-Turn Loop, Tool Error Recovery, Continuation Nudges & Termination
356:  - As soon as the agent emits a final text response (`is_final_response()`) or finishes the current `run_async` turn with `context.patch_submitted == True`, **the harness immediately breaks out of the agent loop** and proceeds to patch extraction and Phase 2 verification.
371:## 6. Built-In Tools Reference (`swegemma.tools`)
384:### 6.1. Execution & Lifecycle Tools (`swegemma/tools/execution.py`)
437:### 6.2. Workspace File Tools (`swegemma/tools/workspace.py`)
488:### 6.3. Code Intelligence Graph Tools (`swegemma/tools/graph.py`)
506:- **Query Resolution Note**: Because the sandbox runs offline without a live neural embedding server, `search_similar_code` resolves `query` against node keys/suffixes stored in the graph and `.npz` dictionary and computes cosine similarity across all other nodes in the repository (with a lexical token-overlap fallback if `query` is a multi-word keyword string). Pass a dotted symbol path or short symbol name (e.g., `"pkg.module.Class.method"`, `"Class.method"`, or `"parse_header"`).
538:## 7. Budgets, Operational Limits & Context Management
540:### 7.1. Default Budgets (`EvaluationBudget`), `eval_config.yaml` & Harness Limits (`HarnessLimits`)
560:| **Verification `pytest` Timeout (Phase 2)** | `config.harness.verification_timeout_seconds` | `300` sec | — *(fixed at `300` sec on scorer)* | `SWE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS` (`metric.py`) |
568:### 7.2. Automatic Context Window Compaction & Prefix Caching
